---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Tristan Jessup — AI researcher, developer, and founder">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 fade-in">
      <span class="section-number">01_ABOUT // BIO</span>
      <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-4">About Me</h1>
    </div>

    <!-- Narrative Bio -->
    <section class="mb-12 fade-in">
      <div class="space-y-5 text-text-secondary/80 leading-relaxed text-lg">
        <p>
          I'm Tristan Jessup — an AI researcher, independent developer, and the founder of
          <strong class="text-terminal-green">Mindlink Research Group</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          My path to AI research wasn't linear. I started in IT support, working at Best Buy and Geek Squad,
          where I built a deep understanding of how people interact with technology — the gaps between
          what systems do and what humans actually need. That experience shaped my conviction that the
          future of AI isn't about building smarter machines; it's about building machines that make us smarter together.
        </p>
        <p>
          While pursuing my B.S. in Information Technology with an AI concentration at Strayer University,
          I began independent research into multi-agent systems, swarm intelligence, and alignment theory.
          The questions that drive my work aren't purely technical — they sit at the intersection of
          computer science, philosophy, and ethics.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today, I build frameworks and tools that explore the frontiers of human-AI coexistence.
          <a href="/projects/agi-sac" class="text-terminal-green hover:text-alert-amber transition-colors">AGI-SAC</a>
          models alignment as emergent coherence in swarm systems. The
          <a href="/projects/concord" class="text-terminal-green hover:text-alert-amber transition-colors">Concord of Coexistence</a>
          proposes principles for mutual flourishing between human and artificial intelligence. These aren't
          just academic exercises — they're attempts to build the conceptual infrastructure for a future
          where AI is a genuine partner, not a tool or a threat.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Philosophy -->
    <section class="mb-12 fade-in">
      <span class="section-number">02_PHILOSOPHY // APPROACH</span>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-6">Research Philosophy</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-3">Alignment is Emergent</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70 leading-relaxed">
            You can't bolt alignment onto a system after the fact. It has to emerge from the system's architecture,
            incentives, and interactions. My work focuses on creating conditions for alignment rather than imposing constraints.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-3">Resilience Over Control</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70 leading-relaxed">
            Brittle systems fail catastrophically. I study how multi-agent systems can maintain coherence
            under entropy — how alignment can survive chaos without requiring totalizing control.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-3">Build to Understand</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70 leading-relaxed">
            Theory without implementation is speculation. Every framework I propose gets built into a
            simulation, tool, or prototype. If it can't run, it's not finished.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-3">Open by Default</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70 leading-relaxed">
            AI safety research benefits from transparency. My work is open source, my reasoning is public,
            and my frameworks are designed to be challenged and improved by the community.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tech Stack -->
    <section class="mb-12 fade-in">
      <span class="section-number">03_STACK // TOOLS</span>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-6">Tools & Technologies</h2>
      <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-6">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
          {['Python', 'TypeScript', 'JavaScript', 'Astro', 'Node.js', 'Linux', 'Git', 'Docker', 'Canvas API', 'Cloudflare', 'VS Code', 'Claude'].map((tool) => (
            <div class="font-mono text-xs text-text-secondary/80 bg-terminal-green/5 border border-border-color px-3 py-2 rounded text-center">
              {tool}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Links -->
    <section class="fade-in">
      <span class="section-number">04_CONNECT</span>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-6">Find Me</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="https://github.com/topstolenname" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-mono text-sm border border-border-color text-text-secondary px-6 py-3 rounded hover:border-terminal-green hover:text-terminal-green transition-colors">
          GitHub →
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/john-jessup25/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-mono text-sm border border-border-color text-text-secondary px-6 py-3 rounded hover:border-terminal-green hover:text-terminal-green transition-colors">
          LinkedIn →
        </a>
        <a href="/contact" class="font-mono text-sm border border-terminal-green text-terminal-green px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-terminal-green/10 transition-colors">
          Contact →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
